       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 600 mg once daily is three times the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day. At that dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and severe GI or bleeding effects. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function, no allergies) would justify a dose that high.\n\nCould this be a typo? Here are some common options:\n- **50 mg daily** is the usual starting dose for depression, GAD, or PTSD. Some indications start lower, at 25 mg.\n- **100 mg or 200 mg daily** is a typical titrated or maximum dose.\n- **600 mg total** might have been meant as a cumulative figure, or the order might be for a different drug.\n\nIf you do intend 600 mg daily, for example under a specialist protocol, tell me and give me the clinical rationale to put in the order note. I'll enter it with that note. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
